00:34:10.320 --> 00:34:29.420
Nick: the view that part of the thing we're trying to find out in this POC, Eric, was to actually find out, like, what was that user experience like, and we've obviously got some feedback forms that we're still going through that came in, so actually, we got it into… we worked on the least friction possible, was really the way that we went about this, just to show

243
00:34:29.560 --> 00:34:45.009
Nick: what it could do, and I think that, from my own experience, credentials and wallets, they often put technology at the forefront, and I guess we're ultimately trying to hide them somewhat to make sure that people didn't actually really know even what they were using.

244
00:34:45.010 --> 00:34:53.519
Nick: So it was just trying to make it as simple as possible, and that's, like I said, the reason that we went, you know, to get… even just remove one click.

