00:37:26.650 --> 00:37:36.590
Nick: You know, that might be a way around, actually even needing a kind of wallet there. But, of course it needs, those companies to want to play ball and…

261
00:37:36.720 --> 00:37:47.280
Nick: although I don't have direct experience, I understand that they would, certainly be keen to charge for the distribution that they could provide, but I think that that would potentially get away from

262
00:37:47.410 --> 00:37:53.949
Nick: needing to come outside of the actual dialing on your phone, but I think it would be probably a long time to get that implemented.

263
00:37:54.820 --> 00:37:58.839
Glyn Povah: Yeah, and I think there's the privacy angle as well. I mean, we probably could do it…

264
00:37:59.060 --> 00:38:04.640
Glyn Povah: in a more B2B, way, without involving the customer.

265
00:38:05.030 --> 00:38:09.180
Glyn Povah: Maybe not necessarily using verifiable credentials,

266
00:38:09.360 --> 00:38:16.099
Glyn Povah: But I think, you know, one of the things we wanted to discover and demonstrate in the POC was that actually the customer is at the center of

